<!--
  Synthetic C-CDA Immunizations section. No patient data.

  The narrative table is ordered Immunization, Administration Dates, Next Due,
  one row per vaccine with every date it was given, so reading it by position
  (vaccine, date, lot) stores the next due date as the lot number and keeps
  one dose of several. The entries carry every dose and field explicitly:

    imm-display      CVX code with a displayName; lot; manufacturer; dose
                     number; route; site; performer and organization
    imm-second-dose  a second dose of the same vaccine, from the same row
    imm-original     CVX code whose originalText references the narrative cell
    imm-name         no code: the product's <name>
    imm-code-only    nothing but the CVX code names it
    imm-planned      moodCode INT: planned, not given
    imm-refused      negationInd: not given
    imm-unnamed      nothing names it, and its text references its own row

  imm-display and imm-second-dose reference one row; imm-original, imm-name
  and imm-unnamed reference their own.
-->
